🎯 Tera First Task
Task 1 — Triggers Practice
Ek repo bana (ya existing use kar), aur ye 3 alag alag workflows bana:
File 1: .github/workflows/on-push.yml
yamlname: On Push Trigger
on:
  push:
    branches: [ main ]
jobs:
  hello:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Say Hello
        run: echo "Triggered by PUSH on main!"
File 2: .github/workflows/on-pr.yml
yamlname: On PR Trigger
on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]
jobs:
  hello:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Say Hello
        run: echo "Triggered by PULL REQUEST!"
File 3: .github/workflows/manual.yml
yamlname: Manual Trigger
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      environment:
        description: 'Which environment?'
        required: true
        default: 'dev'
jobs:
  hello:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Say Hello
        run: echo "Manually triggered for ${{ github.event.inputs.environment }}"

✅ Kya observe karna hai?

Push karo → on-push.yml trigger ho
PR banao → on-pr.yml trigger ho
Actions tab → manual.yml → Run workflow button dikhega → input doge → run hoga


-----------------------------------------------------------

NOW BEFORE MOVING ON WRITING A WORKFLOW WE NEED TO UNDERSTAND THE PROCEESS TO WRITE ANY WORKFLOW

-----------------------------------------------------------


Steps to memorize to write any workflow

🧠 GitHub Actions = 5 Questions
Jab bhi workflow likhna ho, bas ye 5 sawaal khud se pucho:
1. NAME    → Is workflow ka naam kya hai?
2. ON      → Kab chalega? (push/PR/manual/schedule)
3. JOBS    → Kaunsa kaam karna hai? (ek ya multiple?)
4. RUNS-ON → Kahan chalega? (ubuntu/windows/mac)
5. STEPS   → Step by step kya karna hai?
Bas itna! Poora workflow inhi 5 ka answer hai.

🏗️ Structure hamesha same rehta hai
name: (workflow ka naam)

on: (trigger)

jobs:
  (job-naam):
    runs-on: (machine)
    steps:
      - name: (step naam)
        run: (command)
          OR
        uses: (action)

✍️ Likhne ka order
1. Pehle "on" socho    → kab trigger hoga
2. Phir "jobs" socho   → kya kaam karna hai
3. Phir "steps" socho  → ek ek step kya hogi
4. "runs-on" default   → ubuntu-latest almost hamesha
5. "name" last me      → jo chahe rakh do

🔑 Sirf 2 tarah ke steps hote hain
yaml# Type 1 — Command run karo
- name: Kuch bhi
  run: echo "hello"

# Type 2 — Kisi ka banaya action use karo
- name: Kuch bhi
  uses: actions/checkout@v4







