Level 2 - Task 2 — Conditional Steps (if:)
-----------------------------------------------------------

Use conditions to control which steps run based on context.

Common Conditions:

1) Branch check
   if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
   Use: Run only when push happens on main branch

2) Event type check
   if: github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'
   Use: Run only when manually triggered

3) Input check
   if: github.event.inputs.environment == 'production'
   Use: Run only when production environment is selected

4) Actor check
   if: github.actor == 'sidsingh0905'
   Use: Run only when triggered by a specific user

5) Status functions (most important):
   if: failure()  → runs when previous step fails (cleanup/rollback)
   if: always()   → runs regardless of pass or fail (notifications)
   if: success()  → runs only when all previous steps pass (deploy)

Key Learnings:
- failure() and always() override the default skip behaviour
- Use exit 1 to intentionally fail a step for testing
- Combine conditions: if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && github.event_name == 'push'





